From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Smith <74526874+tylertms@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:32:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nouveau): unload GSP at power-off as a PM transition to
 level 3, as nouveau's suspend path does

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/gsp.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/gsp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/gsp.c
index 7e8727ac2288bd72cc975a65b9682eae45ce912d..7f49dd8220a029468e23cd9e4ae3c2659da3d742 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/gsp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/gsp/rm/r535/gsp.c
@@ -1866,7 +1866,15 @@ r535_gsp_fini(struct nvkm_gsp *gsp, enum nvkm_suspend_state suspend)
 	if (READ_ONCE(gsp->dead))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	ret = r535_gsp_rpc_unloading_guest_driver(gsp, suspend);
+	/*
+	 * A power-off unloads as a PM transition to level 3, the arguments
+	 * nouveau's shutdown sent through nouveau_do_suspend() before it
+	 * unloaded at power-off directly; nothing is saved to resume from.
+	 * GSP-RM never answered a level-0 unload sent with the device and its
+	 * channels still initialised (level 0 is what upstream sends only on
+	 * driver removal, after every engine and client is torn down).
+	 */
+	ret = r535_gsp_rpc_unloading_guest_driver(gsp, true);
 	if (WARN_ON(ret))
 		return ret;
 
